<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41422" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rēstĭtūtor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				restorer</i>, <i>rebuilder.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templorum omnium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 4,
					20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1103</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salutis meae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Mil. 15, 39</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 1, 43</span></i> and 61: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reipublicae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Eum. Grat. Act. ad Constant. 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Galliarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vop. Aur. 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tanti operis restitutor deus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Herm. Trism. p. 92</span></i>
			.</div>
